# Samsung vendor guards — Galaxy M31, kernel 4.14.113 (M315FXXS4CWK8)
#
# AUDITED against the device's own /proc/config.gz on 2026-09-02. Only symbols
# that actually exist in THIS tree are listed. The long generic list this file
# used to carry was mostly dead weight: RKP, KDP, PROCA, TIMA, ALWAYS_ENFORCE,
# SEC_RESTRICT_*, KNOX_KAP and DDAR are not defined by this kernel at all.
#
# Already off in the stock config, so nothing to do:
#   CONFIG_UH, CONFIG_UH_LKM_BLOCK, CONFIG_FIVE
#
# Merged after the device defconfig so it wins.

# DEFEX blocks privileged execution outside Samsung's allow-list. Stock: =y.
# CONFIG_SECURITY_DEFEX is not set

# Samsung's device-security telemetry LSM. Stock: =y.
# CONFIG_SECURITY_DSMS is not set

# Samsung Sensitive Data Protection: extends fscrypt in ways Ubuntu Touch's
# own encryption does not expect. Stock: =y.
# CONFIG_SDP is not set
# CONFIG_FSCRYPT_SDP is not set
# CONFIG_ECRYPTFS_FEK_INTEGRITY is not set

# Verified boot on a modified system. Stock: =y.
# CONFIG_DM_VERITY is not set

# Knox network telemetry hooks. Stock: =y. Not a boot blocker, but it has no
# business running under a non-Samsung userspace.
# CONFIG_KNOX_NCM is not set

# NOTE: CONFIG_TZDEV (TrustZone driver) is left ENABLED on purpose — the
# hardware keystore and several vendor HALs talk to it. Disabling it is a
# later experiment, not a bring-up step.
